> f(x: u32 in 0..1000) = x where x < 100
> equiv f f
f and f are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
  domain: x in 0..99 by the where clause (100 points enumerated)
> g(x: u32) = x << 32
> equiv g g
g and g: vacuously equal: the domain has no points to compare
> k(x: u32) = x / 0
> equiv k k
k and k: vacuously equal: the domain has no points to compare
